  "findings": {
    "views": "Eight views is the Pareto point in this seed: +0.10 Acc and +0.94 AP points versus baseline, 67.3% lower latency, and 58.1% lower rank allocation. The changed random-view stream prevents claiming a universal metric gain.",
    "steps": "One step is effectively tied in Acc, improves AP by 0.59 point, and cuts latency 46.4% versus two steps. Three steps loses 0.09 Acc and 0.33 AP point while adding 48.5% latency. Extra tuning steps are not justified.",
    "selection": "Two views is too aggressive. Four nearly matches six. Eight gives a clean +0.03 Acc/+0.14 AP point gain for +1.7% latency. Twelve gives only another +0.05/+0.08 point over eight and its timing is contaminated; eight is the practical selected-view setting.",
    "entropy": "Averaged entropy beats pointwise by 0.43 Acc and 0.50 AP points, mainly through real-image Accuracy.",
    "ois": "OIS improves Acc by 0.84 and fake Accuracy by 2.25 points but reduces AP by 1.04 points versus OIS-off. Keep it for balanced thresholded Accuracy, not as an AP-maximizing claim.",
    "memory": "Rank allocation scales strongly with view count: 3.53/5.17/8.44 GiB for 8/16/32 views. Step and selection-count changes do not materially change the 32-view allocation peak."
